── NOTCH BOOK (#324): the book each one-notch reopen would buy (cleared + that notch's cohort), every name equal-weight, held 8y ──
  cleared    n=1707   book +13.4%/yr  excess +5.1  win 79%  worst -15.1  OOS +7.6/+2.7  top10 +5.5/-15.1
  (n = samples: the cleared book's own, or what the notch adds. `excess`/`bar` are the UNCAPPED book — every admit bought at full weight — kept for continuity with (#324)..(#329). (#330): THE `ship` VERDICT DECIDES AND IT IS READ AT top10 (excess/worst, and the cleared row is the baseline it is measured against), the basket the journaled verdict publishes, where a cohort name must OUTRANK an incumbent to be bought: excess >= that column's `bar`, the p95 of 200 same-n cohorts drawn at random from the refused pool, cutoff-matched and entered at the cohort's own ranks, AND worst >= cleared -1.0, at 20y, 12y and 8y. `inert` = the cohort never reaches the published basket, so the notch changes nothing the tool prints — not a pass, and not a cost it was charged for through (#329). `bar n/a` = the null could not match the cohort's shape, so the row falls back to (#324)'s flat -0.1. `track` grades the same cohorts forward)

── PROXY BOOK (#327): the cleared book split by where its history came from, every name equal-weight, held 8y ──
  own history  n=1707   book +13.4%/yr  excess +5.1  win 79%  worst -15.1  OOS +7.6/+2.7
  (n = samples. Guard, pre-registered: a borrowed-history name must leave the book no worse — excess >= -0.1 and worst >= -1.0 against the own-history row, at 20y, 12y and 8y. Keeps (#324)'s flat bar: this row SPLITS the cleared book rather than admitting out of the refused pool, so (#329)'s matched-n null does not describe it)

── SECTOR BOOK (#328): what a top-1-per-GICS-sector door would add to the cleared book, every name equal-weight, held 8y ──
  cleared      n=1707   book +13.4%/yr  excess +5.1  win 79%  worst -15.1  OOS +7.6/+2.7  top10 +5.5/-15.1
  (n = samples: the cleared book's own, or what the door adds. Cohort is the PREVIOUS cutoff's stocks, backstopped at the index's own 5y CAGR. `excess`/`bar` are the UNCAPPED book; (#330) the `ship` verdict decides and is read at top10 (excess/worst), the published basket — excess >= that column's `bar`, the p95 of 200 same-n refused cohorts entered at the cohort's own ranks, AND worst >= cleared -1.0, at 20y, 12y and 8y. `inert` = the door's names never reach the published basket)
  all entries (SIZED)          book +14.2%/yr  excess +5.8  win 88%  worst -15.1  OOS +7.4/+4.3   (windows 67, deployed 100%) [diagnostic: the book `size` funds, top-25; remainder earns the index]

── CORR-CAP probe: greedy top-10 by growth_score, skip names correlating >= cap with the kept book (36mo trailing), held 8y ──
  cap  off  book +13.9%/yr  excess +5.5  win 85%  worst -15.1  OOS +6.5/+4.5  [cap off = plain top-10 book]
  cap  0.8  book +14.0%/yr  excess +5.6  win 85%  worst -15.1  OOS +6.7/+4.5
  cap  0.6  book +14.2%/yr  excess +5.9  win 85%  worst -15.1  OOS +7.2/+4.6
  cap  0.4  book +14.3%/yr  excess +5.9  win 85%  worst -15.6  OOS +7.4/+4.5
  (a cap lifting book or worst with OOS both + -> ship as a book-construction rule; expectation low — every structure tweak since round 14 diluted.)

Caveats:
  • Peer-relative (#1): returns are de-meaned per ~6mo cutoff, so rho is SELECTION vs same-period
    peers (regime beta removed). A near-empty bucket has a weak peer set -> its rows count for less.
  • In-sample: knobs were hand-tuned on today's data; even the OOS split shares the regime.
  • Survivorship (#5): the universe is names that SURVIVED to today — dead tickers never enter,
    so realized returns are biased UP. Treat the edge as optimistic. Re-run with `stress` to inject losers.
  • Price-only (#6): no as-of P/E reconstructed, so the `value` multiplier is ×1.0 here; as-of DIVIDENDS are live since #53 and every dividend row below is real.
  • Overlapping 6-mo windows share price paths -> samples aren't independent; rho is directional.
  • Long-horizon (MAX monthly): only names alive for the FULL 8y window enter, so
    survivorship bias is WORSE than the daily path, and vol/MA are monthly-bar approximations.
backtest: 200 tickers, WALK-FORWARD scoring every ~6mo with a 8y forward holdout each (MAX monthly history)…